Here are the two files:

**`SortableList.razor`** — The markup with a `@typeparam TItem`, rendering each item via `ItemTemplate` with Move Up/Down buttons (disabled at boundaries).

**`SortableList.razor.cs`** — The `partial class` code-behind:
- Copies `Items` into a private `_items` list in `OnParametersSet` (never mutates the original).
- `MoveUp`/`MoveDown` swap elements in the internal copy, then invoke `OnOrderChanged` with the new list as `IReadOnlyList<TItem>`.

Usage matches your example — just note the callback signature is `EventCallback<IReadOnlyList<TItem>>`:

